%% HOW EVERY NUMBER IN THIS POC WAS MEASURED - and what the two VMs are for.
%%
%% The VMs are TEST HARNESS, not part of the proposed architecture. Nothing the
%% customer would deploy depends on them. They exist because of three facts:
%%   1. 50 RPS x ~1.3 MB mean response is ~65 MB/s sustained. That is not
%%      measurable over a consumer internet link - the link would be the result.
%%   2. Tenant policy forced private-only endpoints on every data store, so the
%%      benchmark had to run INSIDE the VNet. There was no public path to test.
%%   3. Co-locating the load generator with the API would send multi-megabyte
%%      responses over loopback at memory speed, hiding the network entirely,
%%      and the generator's CPU would compete with the API's.
flowchart TB
    OP["Operator workstation<br/>outbound SSH BLOCKED by policy<br/>so every VM action goes through<br/><i>az vm run-command invoke</i>"]

    subgraph VNET["POC VNet - same Azure region as every data store"]
        direction TB
        subgraph COMPUTE["snet-compute"]
            LOAD["<b>vm-orderjsonpoc-load</b><br/>D4s_v5, 4 vCPU<br/><b>WHY: the load generator</b><br/>open-model, constant arrival rate<br/>latency = scheduled-to-complete<br/>so queueing shows up in the number"]
            APIVM["<b>vm-orderjsonpoc-api</b><br/>D8s_v5, 8 vCPU<br/><b>WHY: hosts the API under test</b><br/>FastAPI, 8 uvicorn workers<br/>one STORAGE_BACKEND at a time<br/>/health asserted before every run"]
        end
        subgraph PE["snet-data - private endpoints 10.60.2.0/24"]
            SQL[("Azure SQL Database")]
            COSN[("Cosmos DB for NoSQL")]
            COSM[("Cosmos DB for MongoDB")]
            ADLS[("ADLS Gen2 archive")]
        end
    end

    OP -->|"run-command: start API,<br/>run sweep, fetch results"| LOAD
    OP -->|"run-command"| APIVM
    LOAD ==>|"HTTP over a REAL NIC<br/>accelerated networking<br/>multi-MB responses cross the wire"| APIVM
    APIVM --> SQL
    APIVM --> COSN
    APIVM --> COSM
    APIVM --> ADLS

    RES["Result JSON per run<br/>fetched to results/fulldoc/<br/>then summarised by tooling.<br/><b>No figure is typed by hand.</b>"]
    LOAD --> RES

    subgraph PROOF["What the two-VM split PROVED that one VM could not"]
        direction TB
        X1["Cosmos Mongo sustained 240.8 MB/s<br/>at 4.86 MB payloads, 49.6 RPS"]
        X2["Both SQL designs flattened at ~150 MB/s<br/>with rate falling to ~31 RPS"]
        X3["SAME two machines, SAME API process<br/>=> the SQL ceiling is NOT the network.<br/>It is the client driver's path for<br/>large values."]
        X1 --> X3
        X2 --> X3
    end
    RES -.-> PROOF

    classDef vm fill:#e3f2fd,stroke:#1565c0,stroke-width:2px
    classDef store fill:#f3e5f5,stroke:#6a1b9a
    classDef proof fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32
    class LOAD,APIVM vm
    class SQL,COSN,COSM,ADLS store
    class X1,X2,X3 proof
